\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Example for QM/MM setup: $Au_n@TiO_2$. The adsorbed cluster and direct substrate vicinity defines the QM-region. The far field surrounding (grey particles) pictures a monopole field with formal charges (4+ for Ti and 2- for O). In the blue region, oxygen particles are still represented as monopoles, however Ti-cations are described with ionic pseudopotentials.\relax }}{175}{figure.caption.45}}
\newlabel{fig:qmmm_embedding}{{3.3}{175}{Example for QM/MM setup: $Au_n@TiO_2$. The adsorbed cluster and direct substrate vicinity defines the QM-region. The far field surrounding (grey particles) pictures a monopole field with formal charges (4+ for Ti and 2- for O). In the blue region, oxygen particles are still represented as monopoles, however Ti-cations are described with ionic pseudopotentials.\relax }{figure.caption.45}{}}
